 g\n\n B16\n\n About \n\n Speaker : Professor Atinuke Adediran (Associate P
 rofessor of Law\, Fordham University School of Law\, USA)\n Abstract :  C
 orporate law commonly treats disclosure as a means of providing informatio
 n to investors and shareholders. This seminar asks what disclosure does wh
 en corporations speak about racial inequality. Drawing on Disclosureland's
  original empirical study of statements\, pledges\, and regulatory filings
  from more than 2\,000 companies\, the book shows that corporate words ope
 rate as tools of governance\, shaping what firms recognize\, measure\, fun
 d as philanthropic endeavors\, and ultimately choose to withdraw. Focusing
  on the proliferation of corporate racial-equity commitments after 2020 an
 d their subsequent softening\, narrowing\, or disappearance\, the sem
END:VEVENT
